From f18c3bfc39601f7a83279aabc31d03011e805975 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 16:55:37 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(inventory): confirm survival offhand transfers from
 Bedrock

Retain normal offhand and cursor transactions for client-authoritative inventory sessions. Wait for the authoritative offhand or inventory update before changing the Java cursor, and reopen inventory for recovery when confirmation times out. Keep unsupported clicks on the synthetic cursor from sending requests the server cannot validate.

Use the general request translation from the inventory owner when START_GAME negotiates server-authoritative inventory. Earlier native experiments mixed request slot zero with the offhand content index and tried slot one without a bound player inventory, so their validation errors do not establish that modern offhand requests are unsupported. Native validation of the corrected bound-inventory flow remains pending.

Request full inventory snapshots after a legacy transfer times out.
Reopening the player inventory does not guarantee the cursor and equipment
updates needed to finish recovery. Share the native InventoryMismatch
refresh used by server-authoritative inventory recovery.

Block recipe placement during pending legacy offhand transfers, recovery,
and synthetic cursor ownership. Extend the shared recipe readiness guard
at this patch, where the legacy state becomes available, so furnace and
crafting placement cannot race an unconfirmed offhand operation.

Keep client-authoritative authored menu actions behind the same pending
legacy offhand/cursor and recovery ownership checks. Reject activation
while a prior transfer owns the inventory, preserve an already active
presentation while its action waits, and always permit deactivation.
Verify the actual native control channel, rejected activation status,
and separation from the authoritative request session in a packet test.
